From 18ab2023937a2917af16aed3ff7ac4b46c820ab2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 20:44:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Make Analytics sections transparent, let users pick which two skills to compare

Cards on Analytics (skill comparison, portfolio outcomes, daily activity,
outcomes-resolution) were wrapped in surface-glass-1 panels that don't match
the rest of the dashboard's flat aesthetic. Strip that styling so the
sections sit directly on the page background.

The skill comparison table rendered every skill across every installed
product at once, which just meant a long scroll once more than a
handful of skills were installed. Replace it with a two-picker UI where
the user chooses which two skills to actually look at side by side,
defaulting to the busiest two.

Also hide the generic Work secondary sidebar on /dashboard/analytics —
the page is a self-contained overview with nothing to navigate between,
same treatment already given to Library and Teammates.

Along the way, fix a fifth instance of a recurring bug: the skill
comparison table labeled products via a Showtime/Reputation-Manager-only
ternary, silently mislabeling Cold Open skills. Replaced with a proper
PRODUCT_LABEL map.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
